{"qid":"Q794","names":["Islamic Republic of Iran"],"title":"Islamic Republic of Iran","endonym":{"native":"ایران","lang":"fa"},"capsule":"The Islamic Republic of Iran was established in April 1979 following the revolution that overthrew Shah Mohammad Reza Pahlavi, creating a system of government blending an elected presidency and parliament with ultimate clerical authority vested in the Supreme Leader, first Ayatollah Ruhollah Khomeini (d. 1989) and then Ali Khamenei. The republic's formative decades were shaped by the 1980–88 Iran-Iraq War, which cost an estimated half million lives, and by sustained international confrontation over its nuclear programme, leading to the 2015 JCPOA agreement and its subsequent collapse. It remained the dominant power in a regional network of aligned militias and proxy forces extending from Lebanon to Yemen.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. The territorial extent of the Islamic Republic is fully attested by modern administrative records, international boundaries recognized by the UN, and satellite mapping; no ambiguity attaches to its borders with Iraq, Turkey, the Gulf states, or the Caspian neighbours.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: Iran","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Iran"}],"britannica":"place/Iran","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Iran","rulers":[{"qid":"Q382369","name":"Mehdi Bazargan","start":1979,"end":1979,"image":"PM Bazargan photographed during a Television program - 1979.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/PM%20Bazargan%20photographed%20during%20a%20Television%20program%20-%201979.jpg?width=320","imageLic